					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/psul" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2156983); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2156983&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607633126" alt="psul" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2156983)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/psul" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2156983); return false;" >psul</a></span> <span class="odate time_1490364882 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Mar 2017 14:14</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2774730">
									

<p>Here is my entry for the 3000 contest. I hope that you enjoy it - for particular values of &quot;enjoy&quot;.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Acknowledgements</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Soon&nbsp;that&nbsp;hot&nbsp;wind&nbsp;will&nbsp;come&nbsp;roaring&nbsp;down&nbsp;out&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;black&nbsp;and&nbsp;rip&nbsp;time's&nbsp;skin&nbsp;right&nbsp;off</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A huge number of people reviewed this draft, and I am very grateful to everyone for their help and thoughts.</p>
<ul>
<li>Thank you for review and comment to:
<ul>
<li>sirpudding, for being the first to show support and get the ball rolling, and for being the first person to spot the actual ending before publication.</li>
<li>shaggydredlocks, for helping restructure the logs and coming up with ideas for the ending. May trapdoor spiders never make nests in your throat as you sleep.</li>
<li>Skerples, for some hard truths and for suggesting &quot;The Creepy Meat Cave: an Agent Cooper and Agent Rey story (now featuring Catalan Slang and Banter)&quot; as an alternative title.</li>
<li>Petrograd, for forcing me to reconsider pacing and ditch the drone camera.</li>
<li>djkaktus, for giving me a vote of confidence on chat, and for realising that the draft was screaming at you.</li>
<li>Bluemorpho, for becoming mildly obsessed with the draft and making some good suggestions - sorry I didn't do anything to undermine that trope a bit more.</li>
<li>Communism will win, for realising that this wasn't random bullshit like you're expecting.</li>
<li>Hercules Rockefeller, for very detailed review, and for reading and re-reading the various alternate endings this had in the drafting process.</li>
<li>DrMagnus and many others for reading this on chat and providing your thoughts. Sorry if I've forgotten to mention anyone!</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>The use of human spines for limbs was inspired by <a href="https://tapastic.com/episode/255864">this wonderful image</a> at &quot;Behind You&quot;, which I am linking mostly to encourage everyone to go and read all of that webcomic. Seriously, it's terrific.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Image&nbsp;attribution</a></div>
