			<div class="content" id="post-content-2781408">
									

<blockquote>
<p>I didn't really feel like I needed the SCP-3000-1 or several of the individual entries in the logs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As I mentioned to Scorpion451 above, I felt like the -1s were needed to give a &quot;face&quot; the anomaly - a distinctive entity to focus on (and ideally a creepy one). I'd be interested to hear which of the logs are superfluous, however - I didn't get much feedback on them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>but the final long sells it well. Particularly in describing the oily fat and the descriptions of texture. Texture is the bessst. Upvoted heartily, with incredible glee! It truly made me smile! :)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Thanks! I am a fan of trying to get texture and smells across in writing - they're the things I find most vivid when I'm reading.</p>

